 "_comment": [
  "Verdicts of the fleet gates' Python checks as committed at",
  "the last commit before the fleet switch -- the gate-axes.sh and gate-compliance.sh heredocs",
  "over the shared catalog reader then in fleet/lib, and gate-implementations.sh's fact-capture",
  "check -- measured by running them over each case; never hand-derived. Each",
  "{expr!r} was rewritten to render values the way pycompat.Render does.",
  "\"could-not-run\" is a crash or the heredocs' own exit-2 read failure. Raw",
  "catalogs derive from a live fleet run's .test-output/fleet. Frozen: generated",
  "once by a script that is not kept in the repository."
